{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/36811-demons-in-the-company-of-tremere","id":36811,"title":"Demons in the company of Tremere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-25T00:51:28-08:00","id":36811,"title":"Demons in the company of Tremere","content":"So, the enigmatic Tremere lich.<br /> <br /> What might a meeting between these two beings entail?<br /> <br /> Could a 'Demon Soul' prove particularly useful to a Tremere lich? I've proposed it might even be more well-suited to powering immortality than Mage souls ; or, at least, the possibility of such is worth investigating...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T23:36:20-08:00","id":37197,"title":"","content":"Do demons even have a soul to steal? Perhaps any attempt by a lich to steal a unchained &quot;soul&quot; would end up striping it of it cover giving the lich altering their appearance to match that of the cover it stole. At least until its time to devour another soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1544-vectorfox","name":"VectorFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1544_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T01:49:59-08:00","id":37233,"title":"","content":"I'd let it happen, then treat it as if the demon had just claimed a &quot;soul pact&quot; from the tremere.<br /> Since it's a Tremere it would be of horrid quality, the angel would be in deep dodoo and the mage himself would be wiped out in the process. All rejoice and laugh!<br /> (or, even worse, the Tremere is now a bodyless human that needs to find others to possess, but still capable of making use of his awakened magic)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T02:22:50-08:00","id":37248,"title":"","content":"From how I understand it angels / demons have no souls, only a core.<br /> <br /> Also a soulpact with the tremere is interesting as the teremere can loose that soul quite easily and replace it thus breaking the pact time and again for it needs to be remade then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T02:49:35-08:00","id":37255,"title":"","content":"Soul pacts don't really barter a soul though, they give the unchained the right to burn you out and claim your life as a cover. Up to ST of course but personally I wouldn't allow it to be sidestepped as easily as that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T05:25:56-08:00","id":37280,"title":"","content":"Tehy dont function though without a soul, and if someone looses his soul the soul pact gets suspended or so until he has a soul again if I remember correclty","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T06:02:50-08:00","id":37292,"title":"","content":"Actually it only says the soulless can't _sign_ such a deal, not that it gets suspended <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (unless I'm missing something written in some obscure part of the text)<br /> And in the end it's irrelevant, what is being discussed here is a Tremere trying to &quot;steal&quot; the core of demon, and what might happen to him. No pact required for that backfire, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T06:34:51-08:00","id":37302,"title":"","content":"I don't think Death is sufficient to do such a thing, so Tremere could not do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T10:30:45-08:00","id":37390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/36811-demons-in-the-company-of-tremere?p=37248#post37248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From how I understand it angels / demons have no souls, only a core.<br /> <br /> Also a soulpact with the tremere is interesting as the teremere can loose that soul quite easily and replace it thus breaking the pact time and again for it needs to be remade then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would mean they are pretty easy to identify by supernatural effects that allow one to study a soul, like the Soul Marks spell. So, they probably have something that looks enough like a soul to fool any magics that deal with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T10:36:28-08:00","id":37393,"title":"","content":"Pondering this relationship even further, a number of interesting things occur to me...<br /> <br /> By the standards of the Unchained, a lich is remarkable. The lich does NOT require consent or authorization to tamper with human 'source code'. A demon needs a written bonafide to get 'clearance' to do this sort of thing, owing to inscrutable rules they only vaguely understand, but a Mage can just yank souls out of people. The way a demon would react to this is probably fairly individual ; some might consider it very intriguing, others might consider it very disturbing.<br /> <br /> This only scratches the surface of what a Lich might seem to be however. Consider - the lich is a very, very unique creature from the standpoint of the Unchained. The lich is a piece of Cover that has become so advanced, so 'self aware', that it has literally taken control of the entity it nominally is an organ of. This Cover is not simply a mask, as it is to unchained. Nor is an absolute physical embodiment, like for mortals. This Cover may not understand the God Machine or the true nature of the system but it's more than capable of securing new souls to survive in symbiosis with.<br /> <br /> The -Cover- has taken control of the being completely. Souls are disposable. They come and go, transient. What defines the being is not what is within it, but rather, the Cover, always seeking more soul energy to power it.<br /> <br /> It's... almost like a reverse unchained, isn't it? A being doing very, very similar things from the exact opposite direction?<br /> <br /> ... and that's not even getting into the reverse. What does a lich make of the Unchained? I'll look into that in my next post, when I get around to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T17:37:30-08:00","id":38504,"title":"","content":"Isn't magic that directly tampers with a beings Integrity Trait archmastery? I really doubt demons have their own soul to steal, the closest thing is his Cover. However, I am sure that due to the intimate connection demons have to their cover, they'd notice if someone tried to steal it. Personally, if I felt a lich stealing my soul, it Go Loud and kill them sooner than let him take it peacefully. If the spell is possible, i'd as an ST say if it isnt archmastery, it should have to overcome BOTH Cover and Primum. For me, however, the interesting quetion is more about what a tremere can DO for a demon. Can the same souls that power Tremere be used for Cover (rather than suffering Soullessness, the mortal becomes a Cover)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}